   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "operator_pin_step1_cell2714",
     "description": "The operator identity at the exit state, pinned from cism_thermo.csv step 1, cell (27,14) (the thickest traced cell, thck = 699.2999877929688 m; artm = -9.678254083449986 degC; the step-1 relaxation is the strongest in the window, bed warming by 0.0122 K). Since the CISM step is one backward-Euler solve, (T_exit - T_entry)/dttem = L*T_exit + Phi exactly for the interior rows; dTdt is evaluated at the exit profile (initial_conditions temp = the exit temp_001..010 columns on the interior nodes) with the dumped dissip and asserted against (T_exit - T_entry)/dttem with dttem = 1.5768e7 s on the 10 interior nodes (CISM layers 1..10; the surface and bed nodes are algebraic - the Dirichlet and the basal-BC rows - pinned separately below as temp_sfc/temp_bed, and the interior stencil reads them at the boundary faces). The surface law temp_sfc = min(0, artm) = -9.678254083449986 degC (the exit temp_000), the pmp law bpmp = -0.61283055916793 degC (exit bpmp), the basal matrix row temp_bed = -5.600667536641113 degC (exit temp_011) with btemp_ground_entry = -5.61283055916793 (the entry temp_011; frozen row: the flux-balance condition holds to 6.2e-17 W/m2, far below eps11), the conductive flux lcondflx_ground = -bfricflx = -8.298816394880562e-05 W/m2 and the resulting bmlt_ground = 0 (the dump's bmlt_ground column is 0 on every row; the m/yr dump value is bmlt_ground*scyr) are asserted in the same run. The per-node residuals of the identity are <= 5.1e-10 relative (the dump's 17-digit round-trip and the tridiagonal solve round-off), hence the per-assertion rel 1e-8.",
